    costrows=''.join('<tr><td>'+esc(a)+'</td><td>'+seconds(b)+'</td></tr>' for a,b in costs)
    census=mut['proof_census']
    page=r'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Addition commutativity · external finite-induction control</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="report.css"><script>window.MathJax={tex:{inlineMath:[['\\(','\\)']],displayMath:[['\\[','\\]']]},options:{skipHtmlTags:['script','noscript','style','textarea','pre','code']}};</script><script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-chtml.js"></script><style>main{max-width:1120px;margin:auto;padding:24px}section{margin:38px 0}.formula{overflow:auto;max-width:100%;margin:15px 0}.proof-line{display:grid;grid-template-columns:30px minmax(0,1fr);gap:14px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd;padding:18px 0}.boundary{background:#fff5df;border-left:4px solid #b38843;padding-left:12px}.annotation{font-size:13px;color:#536968}pre{white-space:pre;overflow:auto;max-height:360px;font-size:11px}details{margin:14px 0}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:13px}th,td{padding:10px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #ccd}.scroll{overflow:auto}select{max-width:100%}[hidden]{display:none!important}.flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:12px;margin:24px 0}.flow>div{padding:18px;background:#eef4ee;border-top:3px solid #357f6b}.flow strong{display:block;margin-bottom:8px}@media(max-width:650px){.flow{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style></head><body><main><nav><a href="index.html#goals">Research program</a> · <a href="commutativity_feasibility.html#result">Separate native feasibility gate</a> · <a href="external_left_successor_control.html#reader">Earlier external successor control</a></nav><h1>Addition commutativity: an external control</h1><p>Six fresh E searches find the exact universal target. Every returned proof passes complete independent checking and replay. These are external first-order proofs, not native Wang certificates or GCTS/RL discoveries.</p><div class="formula">__TARGET__</div><p><strong>The same complete five-instance induction union is supplied in every target lane.</strong> It contains both mechanically declared commutativity alternatives, both earlier left-successor alternatives and the zero-left predicate. Theory-only therefore already receives donor induction predicates. This is broader than the native no-transfer finite grammar and restricts native induction to explicit first-order instances.</p><div class="flow"><div><strong>Theory only</strong>No theorem inputs; \(36\) returned lines.</div><div><strong>Zero-left transfer</strong>Uses the transferred zero-left theorem; \(31\) returned lines.</div><div><strong>Both transfers</strong>Uses both transferred theorems; \(26\) returned lines.</div></div><section id="comparison"><h2>What the comparison establishes</h2><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Lane</th><th>Run</th><th>Lines</th><th>Lemma inputs used</th><th>E seconds</th><th>Check seconds</th><th>Replay seconds</th></tr>__ROWS__</table></div><p>Checked theorem inventory shortens E’s printed refutations on this assertion. This is a descriptive result from two same-ordering repetitions, with setup and replay costs charged. It does not establish a universal search advantage, statistical significance or a GCTS/RL contribution. No commutativity target search has yet run in the separate native feasibility milestone.</p><p>The earlier zero-left theorem was automatically discovered by GCTS. The left-successor theorem came from ordinary forward chaining and subsequently passed the larger-workspace native gate. Their exact primitive requests and complete independent native replay authorities are bound here. No unresolved local block interface is supplied to E: the \(93\) pending native admissions remain pending.</p></section><section id="theory"><h2>Exact axioms, instances and transferred statements</h2>__AXIOMS__<p>The arithmetic symbols are uninterpreted under the exported axioms; no finite domain or intended natural-number model is assumed. All parameter closure and binder names are retained.</p>__SCHEMAS__<p>Optional theorem inputs are __LEMMA0__ and __LEMMA1__. Before target execution, two separate fresh E setup searches prove these conclusions from their exact original axiom/finite-instance dependencies. Both returned setup derivations are completely checked and independently replayed. The primitive native proof paths are provenance, not supplied E search paths.</p><p>The original theory remains <code>AZ</code>, <code>AS</code> and native <code>nat-induction</code>. This external control exports exactly the declared five finite instances. It is not full Peano arithmetic, unrestricted schema search or exact equality to the native finite contextual grammar. E may instantiate terms and quantifiers beyond that grammar. A formal speed ratio and native-Wang acceptance claim would be unjustified.</p></section><section id="reader"><h2>Read the actual proofs line by line</h2><p>Each formula below is decoded from the actual returned TSTP line, followed by a literal English translation and its checked parents. Clause variables are explicitly universally closed. Display aliases \(w_i\) are declared per run with exact E names and arities. Amber rows are conservative witness extensions, with their full replacement derivations. These are first-order rows, not drawings of Wang tiles.</p><label for="proof-choice">Actual fresh derivation</label> <select id="proof-choice">__OPTIONS__</select>__PANELS__</section><section id="checking"><h2>Checking and remaining limitations</h2><p>The existing focused and shared-context adapters are unchanged. Every input AST and role, target negation, previous-node parent, witness scope/dependency/arity, fresh-symbol registry and logical consequence is validated. A finite set of exact universal instances can justify a refutation; finite satisfiability never establishes unrestricted quantified entailment. Unsupported proof features remain unknown. No positive conjecture is used as a premise.</p><p>Independent serialized replay covers all \(8\) returned derivations, __LINES__ lines, __BOUNDARIES__ conservative boundaries and __TREES__ focused logical trees. All __CORRUPTIONS__ actual-proof corruptions are rejected. Fresh pre-run gates also retain \(12\) unrestricted-FOL relations, \(13\) altered-instance/tree checks and \(51\) shared-context/witness fixtures, including quantifier-order and finite-domain counterexamples.</p><p>The parser, clausifier and replay implementations are trusted code, not a formally verified kernel. Primary references are the <a href="https://tptp.org/UserDocs/TPTPLanguage/TPTPLanguage.shtml">official TPTP language</a>, E’s <a href="https://github.com/eprover/eprover/blob/3b7afc70fe77d3118bb95144c4735ca45f5f31cf/CLAUSES/ccl_tcnf.c">pinned clausifier implementation</a> and <a href="https://github.com/eprover/eprover/blob/3b7afc70fe77d3118bb95144c4735ca45f5f31cf/README.md">README</a>. E’s bundled <code>checkproof</code> skips nonclausal steps and is not our acceptance basis.</p></section><section id="costs"><h2>Preparation, setup, search and replay costs</h2><table><tr><th>Component</th><th>Seconds</th></tr>__COSTS__</table><p>The producer cap was \(180\) seconds, including fixtures, both setup searches, the pre-target gate and six target runs. Each E process had \(10\) CPU seconds, \(12\) wall seconds and \(1024\) MiB; each certificate worker had \(20\) wall seconds. The existing focused checker retains \(5\) rounds, \(4000\) instances and \(600\) terms, with its own sampled \(1\)-GiB worker RSS cutoff. There were no new unknowns or unexecuted runs.</p><p>Nested costs are not additive. Process check/replay timings include startup and serialization. Inherited proof discovery, native checking, complete replay, implementation effort and the earlier pinned E build are additional costs, retained in their separate reports and exact evidence. They were not rerun or treated as free cold work. Shared-host and warm-cache conditions preclude a controlled speed claim. Earlier native and validator unknowns remain unchanged.</p></section><section id="evidence"><h2>Exact frozen evidence</h2><p><a href="external_commutativity_control_plan.json">Predeclared plan</a> · <a href="external_commutativity_control_summary.json">Compact result and costs</a> · <a href="external_commutativity_control_audit.json">Complete independent audit</a> · <a href="external_commutativity_control_mutations.json">Actual-certificate corruption audit</a> · <a href="external_commutativity_control_data.json.gz">Every input, source, returned node and certificate</a></p><p>The evidence download preserves every private file and every frozen source byte, with SHA-256 bindings. Full theorem request/input/output and native authority records are retained. No target proof sequence or preferred induction variable was supplied. This separate report awaits root publication.</p><details><summary>Reproduce in a fresh private directory with the pinned E binary</summary><pre>PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX=/private/tmp/gcts-native-wang-pycache python3 research/gcts-rl-renewal/external_commutativity_reproduce.py --output .gcts-active/external-commutativity-reproduce --e /private/tmp/gcts-external-eprover-20261011/PROVER/eprover</pre></details></section></main><script>document.getElementById('proof-choice').addEventListener('change',async function(){for(const p of document.querySelectorAll('.proof-panel'))p.hidden=p.id!=='proof-'+this.value;if(window.MathJax?.typesetPromise)await MathJax.typesetPromise([document.getElementById('proof-'+this.value)]);});</script></body></html>'''
    values=dict(TARGET=formula(bundle['spec']['target']),AXIOMS=''.join('<p><code>'+esc(n)+'</code></p><div class="formula">'+formula(f)+'</div>' for n,f in sorted(bundle['spec']['theory']['axioms'].items())),SCHEMAS=schemas,LEMMA0=formula(bundle['lemmas'][0]['formula']),LEMMA1=formula(bundle['lemmas'][1]['formula']),ROWS=''.join(rows),OPTIONS=''.join(options),PANELS=''.join(panels),COSTS=costrows,LINES=num(census['lines']),BOUNDARIES=num(census['boundaries']),TREES=num(census['focused_trees']),CORRUPTIONS=num(len(mut['corruptions'])))
